.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
generic parts of icon-lists. 

right now only used when compiling with specific parts from evas2.c, should replace gnome-icon-list in the future, however. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "static int icon_compare (const void * flags, const void * a, const void * b)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
compare two icons (for sort-order) 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
-1,0,+1 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIflags\fP sort-flags 
.br
\fIa\fP the first icon 
.br
\fIb\fP the second icon
.RE
.PP

.SS "void icon_dst (\fBicon\fP * i)"
.PP
destruct an icon and its elements. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIi\fP - the icon to release
.RE
.PP

.SS "void icon_dst_all (\fBicon\fP * i)"
.PP
destruct an icon and all its successors. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIi\fP - the first icon to release
.RE
.PP

.SS "void icon_el_dst (\fBicon_el\fP * e)"
.PP
destruct an icon-element. 
.PP
if e->data is set, will call \fBicon_el_data_dst()\fP. since the nature of the data is GUI-specific (Evas_Object or such), \fBicon_el_data_dst()\fP is as well. it must be defined in the GUI-specific module. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIe\fP - the element to destruct
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon_el\fP* icon_el_dst_all (\fBicon_el\fP * e)"
.PP
destruct an icon-element and all its successors. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIe\fP - the first element to destruct (normally the first element of the icon)
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon\fP* icon_el_dst_by_tag (\fBicon\fP * i, element_tag t)"
.PP
destruct icon-element by tag. 
.PP
convenience function. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIi\fP - the icon to remove elements from 
.br
\fIt\fP - tag to look for (all matches)
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon_el\fP* icon_el_get_by_tag (\fBicon_el\fP * el, element_tag t, void ** o)"
.PP
find icon-element by tag. 
.PP
convenience function. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIel\fP - first element in list 
.br
\fIt\fP - tag to look for (first match) 
.br
\fIo\fP - where to copy the data-element of the found icon_el, or NULL
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon_el\fP* icon_el_new (icon_state state, int xo, int yo, int w, int h, void * data, void * next)"
.PP
create new icon-element. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIstate\fP - this element should be visible when the icon is in 'state' 
.br
\fIxo\fP - x-offset to icon's upper-left corner (to 'icon-x') 
.br
\fIyo\fP - y-offset to icon's upper-left corner (to 'icon-y') 
.br
\fIw\fP - width of element 
.br
\fIh\fP - height of element 
.br
\fIdata\fP - payload (e.g. an Evas_Object) 
.br
\fInext\fP - next element, or NULL for EOL
.RE
.PP

.SS "void icon_list_destroy (void * il)"
.PP
destruct an icon-list and all its icons. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list to release
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon\fP* icon_list_get_icon_at (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int x, int y)"
.PP
get the icon at a given coordinate 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIx\fP - icon-list relative x (0..) 
.br
\fIy\fP - icon-list relative y (0..)
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon\fP* icon_list_get_icon_by_file (\fBicon_list\fP * il, const char * file)"
.PP
get the icon that represents a given file. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIfile\fP - the file to find the icon for
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon\fP* icon_list_get_icon_by_index (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int in)"
.PP
get icon number 'in'. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIin\fP - the index
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_get_index_at (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int x, int y)"
.PP
find out the index of the icon at a given coordinate 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIx\fP - icon-list relative x (0..) 
.br
\fIy\fP - icon-list relative y (0..)
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_icon_in_rubber (\fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBicon\fP * i)\fC [inline]\fP"
.PP
find out whether icon is in rubber-band selection. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
TRUE if icon is at least partially in the rectangular rubber-band selection. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP -the icon-list 
.br
\fIi\fP - the icon
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon\fP* icon_list_icon_insert (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int index, const char * name, const char * file, const char * label, const char * thumb, void * user1, void * user2, int redraw)"
.PP
insert icon into icon-list. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - icon-list 
.br
\fIindex\fP - insert after index'th icon (0 for 'make first icon in list') 
.br
\fIname\fP - the name of the icon-image ('/foo/bar/binary.png') 
.br
\fIfile\fP - the file represented by the icon ('/bin/ls') 
.br
\fIlabel\fP - the text-label to go underneath the icon-image ('ls') 
.br
\fIthumb\fP - the 'thumbnail' for the file, or NULL ('/home/azundris/.thumbnails/large/ffa4b11d64a9d082c4b8d4e795d9b3e8.png') 
.br
\fIuser1\fP - user-data. in evidence, the stat-info for the icon. 
.br
\fIuser2\fP - user-data. in evidence, the file-info for the icon. 
.br
\fIredraw\fP - redraw icon-list after icon is inserted?
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon\fP* icon_list_icon_insert_sorted (\fBicon_list\fP * il, const char * name, const char * file, const char * label, const char * thumb, void * user1, void * user2, int redraw)"
.PP
determine index, insert icon into icon-list. 
.PP
see \fBicon_list_icon_insert()\fP re the parameters.
.SS "int icon_list_icon_remove (\fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBicon\fP * i, int redraw)"
.PP
remove an icon from the icon-list. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIi\fP - the icon to remove 
.br
\fIredraw\fP - redraw the icon-list after removing the icon?
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_icon_visible (\fBicon_list\fP * il, \fBicon\fP * i)\fC [inline]\fP"
.PP
find out whether icon is exposed. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
TRUE if icon is at least partially in the exposed part of the scroll-area. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP -the icon-list 
.br
\fIi\fP - the icon
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_layout_all (\fBicon_list\fP * il)"
.PP
recalc layout of all icons in list. 
.PP
unless the FR_NOSCROLL-bit is set on the frozen-property, a redraw will be effected calling the efun \fBsb_update()\fP. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon_list\fP* icon_list_new (const char * name, void * theme, void * canvas, int wpad, int hpad, int flags)"
.PP
create new icon-list 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP - name for the icon-list (evidence: 'iconview' or 'shelf') 
.br
\fItheme\fP - the theme for this icon-list 
.br
\fIcanvas\fP - the canvas for this icon-list (GtkGEvas, Evas, ...) 
.br
\fIwpad\fP - horizontal padding between icons 
.br
\fIhpad\fP - vertical padding between icons 
.br
\fIflags\fP - reserved
.RE
.PP

.SS "void icon_list_resized (\fBicon_list\fP * il, long w, long h)"
.PP
adjust size of icon-list. 
.PP
the GUI-part of the icon-list will likely have a callback for when the window's size changes. that callback should in turn call icon_list_resized to let the internal representation know about the change as well. \fBicon_list_resized()\fP will also re-layout the window's contents. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIw\fP - the new width of the icon-list 
.br
\fIh\fP - the new height of the icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_resort (\fBicon_list\fP * il)"
.PP
sort icons in icon-list. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBicon_list\fP* icon_list_rst (\fBicon_list\fP * il)"
.PP
reset icon-list. 
.PP
this throws out all icons and resets settings to 'factory defaults.' in other words, it should be similar to destructing an icon-list and making a new one. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_scroll_abs (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int sx, int sy)"
.PP
scroll icon-list to absolute position. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIsx\fP - the desired horizontal position (0..) 
.br
\fIsy\fP - the desired vertical position (0..)
.RE
.PP

.SS "static int icon_list_scroll_do (\fBicon_list\fP * il)\fC [static]\fP"
.PP
do the actual footwork for the scrolling routines. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_scroll_pg (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int sx, int sy)"
.PP
scroll icon-list page-wise. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIsx\fP - scroll horizontally: <0, page left; 0, don't scroll; >0, page right 
.br
\fIsy\fP - scroll vertically: <0, page up; 0, don't scroll; >0, page down
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_scroll_rel (\fBicon_list\fP * il, int sx, int sy)"
.PP
scroll relative to current position. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIsx\fP - the horizontal offset 
.br
\fIsy\fP - the vertical offset
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_set_separators (\fBicon_list\fP * il, const char * sep)"
.PP
set separators for word-wrap. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list to change the separators on 
.br
\fIsep\fP - a C-string containing the desired separators
.RE
.PP

.SS "static char* make_label (\fBicon_list\fP * il, const char * in)\fC [inline, static]\fP"
.PP
make icon-label with suggested wrap-points. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list (containing a list of separator characters) 
.br
\fIin\fP - the text for the label
.RE
.PP

